      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TOUIE LOUIE NZ (7) is a newcomer to the powerhouse Jason Grimson yard from NZ where he was runner-up two back at Addington. Hasn't raced for a month but looks well placed to kick off in Australia with a win. YA RACIN CARL (8) placed here fresh then overcame a similar barrier to this for a 1.7m win last week at Menangle. Has returned in fine order and could work through his grades now. LOIERO (11) came from this barrier to score last start by 3.7 metres at West Wyalong, his second success from his last three outings. INTERESTINME (9) continued a run of top-four results when beaten less than 4 metres into second here last week. Draws for a trail and could be dangerous.",
